## Runtime image

The container image is built on Alpine Linux and ships nftables,
wireguard-tools and wireguard-go from its package repositories, each under
its own licence (GPL-2.0 for nftables and wireguard-tools, MIT for
wireguard-go). They are separate programs invoked by vpn20, not linked into it.

WireGuard is a registered trademark of Jason A. Donenfeld. vpn20 is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the WireGuard project.
Windows support also uses the official WireGuardNT binary distribution
(license included in Windows packages), WireGuard for Windows Go packages
(MIT), and github.com/tailscale/wf (BSD-3-Clause). These projects retain their
respective copyrights. See the bundled licenses and Go module metadata.

Windows relay also bundles the official signed Wintun binary distribution
(license in licenses/Wintun) and gVisor netstack (Apache-2.0). Their original
license texts are included in the Windows packages.
